        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "The Nil Trap, Structurally"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "var p *MyErr          // nil pointer",
            "var e error = p       // type word is SET",
            "fmt.Println(e == nil) // false"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Non-nil type word plus nil data word = non-nil interface",
            "The number one Go gotcha, and it is pure memory layout"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Dispatch Speed"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "The compiler devirtualizes when it proves the concrete type",
            "PGO improves that since Go 1.21",
            "Assertions compare the stored type pointer or hash — cheap, not free"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "callout",
          "style": "tip",
          "title": "Ground truth",
          "text": "Read `runtime/iface.go`, or inspect the layout with `unsafe`, when you need certainty about a claim."
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Interfaces Inside Interfaces",
          "ink": "accent"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "type ReadWriter interface {",
            "\tReader // method sets union",
            "\tWriter",
            "}"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "`io.ReadWriteCloser` composes three of them",
            "The stdlib's standard composition ladder",
            "Overlapping names legal since Go 1.14 if signatures match"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Types Inside Structs"
        },
        {
          "type": "code",
          "lang": "go",
          "lines": [
            "type Server struct {",
            "\t*log.Logger // field name is Logger",
            "\taddr string",
            "}"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Promotion generates a forwarding method, not inheritance",
            "No virtual dispatch back to the outer type",
            "An embedded method calls the embedded version, never your override"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "page_title": "Promotion Rules & Type Assertions",
      "blocks": [
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Interface In A Struct"
        },
        {
          "type": "bullets",
          "items": [
            "Gives a partial implementation that still compiles",
            "Missing methods panic at call time, not build time",
            "Powers forward-compatible wrappers over `io.Reader`"
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "heading",
          "text": "Name Resolution"
        },
        {
